    "summary": "Evergreen tree native to the Andean valleys of Chile, Peru and Ecuador. Its fruit ripens after falling, developing soft, very sweet, dry and floury orange-yellow flesh around large hard seeds. The ripe fruit is eaten raw or used in Peru to flavour drinks and ice cream, and its flesh can be dried into powder.",
